<title>HONG KONG: AWT World plans air freight JV in China.</title>
<headline>AWT World plans air freight JV in China.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air and seafreight forwarder AWT World Transport Holdings Ltd said it has agreed to form a 70 percent owned air freight forwarding joint venture in China.</p>
<p>AWT World said the joint venture would be 30 percent held by CNAC Trans-World Asia Services Co Ltd, a wholly-owned subsidiary of China National Aviation Corp (Group) Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Details of the terms of the joint venture will be subject to further negotiation between the company and CNAC,&quot; said AWT's company secretary Chang Kin Man in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
